1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,956
Agentic FedGrid: privacy-preserving intrusion detection with federated learning and agentic AI.

2
00:00:07,206 --> 00:00:12,881
By Mohith Kumar M, Anusha B, Lokesh Kumar Yadav and Rohan C Ravi, guided

3
00:00:12,881 --> 00:00:19,974
by Dr. Naidila Sadashiv, Department of ISE, JSS Academy of Technical Education, Bengaluru.

4
00:00:20,224 --> 00:00:26,488
Our objectives: detect attacks on edge devices, so raw traffic never leaves the device.

5
00:00:26,738 --> 00:00:30,580
Learn together across sites through federated learning, and

6
00:00:30,580 --> 00:00:34,682
respond autonomously but safely, even against poisoned updates.

7
00:00:34,932 --> 00:00:40,284
Each edge node runs a tabular Transformer that classifies every network flow.

8
00:00:40,534 --> 00:00:47,086
Nodes train small LoRA adapters, so each upload is about 10 KB instead of 100 KB.

9
00:00:47,336 --> 00:00:52,568
A serverless AWS backend combines these updates into a new global model.

10
00:00:52,818 --> 00:00:59,008
An agent decides whether to ignore, alert or block based on expected cost. Blocks expire

11
00:00:59,008 --> 00:01:04,986
automatically, and a new model is adopted only if it does not hurt local performance.

12
00:01:05,236 --> 00:01:11,188
This lets hospitals, colleges and small businesses share threat knowledge without sharing private

13
00:01:11,188 --> 00:01:16,036
traffic, at low cost, and with fewer false alarms cutting off legitimate users.

14
00:01:16,286 --> 00:01:23,460
On four AWS nodes, the model reaches 87.7% accuracy on the official

15
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:30,206
UNSW-NB15 test set and 99.3% on ToN-IoT, with 1.7 ms inference.

16
00:01:30,456 --> 00:01:39,408
Under poisoning, median aggregation holds 86.5% accuracy, versus 47.5% for plain averaging.

17
00:01:39,658 --> 00:01:46,042
With a simulated analyst, wrongly blocked benign traffic drops from 22% to 2%.

18
00:01:46,292 --> 00:01:51,091
Agentic FedGrid shows that private, autonomous intrusion detection

19
00:01:51,091 --> 00:01:53,708
at the edge is practical. Thank you.

